problems.problem:
Find all functions $f(n)$ having the following three properties:

a) for any natural number $n$, $f(n)$ is also a natural number;

b) $f(n + m) = f(n)f(m)$ holds for any natural numbers $n$ and $m$;

c) the equation $f(f(n)) = (f(n))^2$ has some natural number $n_0$ as its solution.

The game TETRIS is played according to the following rules:

• at the beginning of the game, the "well" of width three squares contains the figures shown in the left part of the figure;

• afterwards only the figures shown in the right part of the figure fall into the "well" one at a time, where every figure can be rotated and shifted while falling, but not reflected;

• if one or more horizontal rows of the "well" become full, all such rows are removed before the next figure falls.

Find the least number of figures after whose falling the "well" can become empty.

